==In animation==
[[File:Team Skull Grunts anime.png|thumb|250px|Team Skull Grunts Rapp (left), Tupp (middle), and Zipp (right) in {{aniseries|SM}}]]
Team Skull Grunts debuted in ''[[SM001|Alola to New Adventure!]]'' when three of them, [[Tupp]], [[Rapp]], and [[Zipp]], were seen harassing {{an|Kiawe}} and then taking him on in a [[Pokémon battle]]. The trio made a bet with Kiawe, saying they would get his {{p|Charizard}} if they won. Kiawe accepted the challenge and then sent out {{TP|Kiawe|Turtonator}}. {{Ash}} and {{AP|Pikachu}} stepped in to assist Kiawe as they felt that what the three grunts were doing was unfair. Kiawe was able to defeat the three grunts by having his Turtonator use the [[Z-Move]] {{m|Inferno Overdrive}}, causing them to retreat. They reappeared in ''[[SM011|Young Kiawe Had a Farm!]]'', using their {{p|Zubat}}, {{p|Salandit}}, and {{p|Garbodor}} to get revenge on Kiawe. However, they were soon defeated by Pikachu's {{m|Gigavolt Havoc}}.

Several Grunts appeared in a flashback in ''[[SM005|Yo, Ho, Ho! Go, Popplio!]]''. They were attacking a {{TP|Lana|Popplio}} when {{an|Lana}} appeared with her {{p|Lapras}} and defeated them with {{m|Ice Beam}}.

In ''[[SM024|Alolan Open House!]]'', Tupp, Rapp, and Zipp attempted to steal three [[Poké Ride|Ride]] {{p|Tauros}}. They then battled {{Ash}} and {{Delia}}, but were soon defeated by Pikachu's Gigavolt Havoc again. 

In ''[[SM025|A Team-on-Team Tussle!]]'', the trio tried to take a [[Darkinium Z]] that was stuck in a mountain, which was being guarded by multiple {{rf|Alolan}} {{p|Rattata}} and {{p|Raticate}}. One of the Raticate was a [[Totem Pokémon]]. They fought against {{TRT}}, who were also trying to take the [[Z-Crystal]]. In the end, Team Rocket ended up with the Darkinium Z. In ''[[SM027|A Glaring Rivalry!]]'', they confronted {{an|Gladion}} in an attempt to steal his {{p|Umbreon}}, but were swiftly defeated by his {{p|Lycanroc}}.

In ''[[SM065|Turning Heads and Training Hard!]]'', Tupp, Rapp, and Zipp, alongside multiple other Team Skull Grunts, arrived at the [[Pokémon School]], where they challenged [[Ilima]] to a battle. However, the Grunts were soon defeated by Ilima's {{p|Eevee}}, who was powered up by {{m|Extreme Evoboost}}.

Multiple Team Skull Grunts appeared in ''[[SM115|The Dealer of Destruction!]]'', with a Grunt named [[Akitoshi]] being among them. They were seen at the [[Shady House]] alongside [[Guzma]] and [[Plumeria]], watching {{an|Professor Kukui}}'s {{al|Pokémon League}} announcement on [[television|TV]] with them.

In ''[[SM128|League Offenders and Defenders!]]'', some Team Skull Grunts attempted to destroy the [[Manalo Stadium]], but they were stopped separately by Team Rocket and Gladion.

In ''[[SM129|Battle Royal 151!]]'', many Team Skull Grunts took part in the [[Battle Royal]] round of the [[Manalo Conference]]. They ganged up on Ilima and his Eevee but were quickly defeated, eliminating them from the competition.

In ''[[SM130|Battling Besties!]]'', many Team Skull Grunts watched and supported Guzma as he battled Ilima during the Manalo Conference though Rapp and two girls were cheering for Ilima.

